// ===================== 9.3 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('9.3  The limitation that strengthens the claim it limits'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Ask for the page number and nothing else.** **In most classes eight of the ten limitations are on the last page of the document**, and that single column of page numbers is the cycle. **Write the ten numbers and the ten document lengths side by side** and let the room read the arithmetic: the limitation is always last, in ten documents of ten different kinds, written by ten people who were never taught to put it there.'));
out.push(A('**b** Strengthen: **3** and **4**. ⚠ **Not 1, 2 or 5**, which name no finding and therefore limit everything above them. **3 and 4 both have a _therefore_ half**: one draws a boundary round what the comparison establishes, and the other says expressly what the absent weld inspection does not weaken. **Make the room find the word _therefore_ or its equivalent in each** — **it is the hinge, and the three weak ones do not contain it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **it reads as a withdrawal of everything above it**, because a limitation with no claim beside it attaches to the whole document.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **He read it to the tribunal twice** — **once to show that Mr Zahreddine was honest and once to show that nothing he had written could be relied upon.**   **2** **By what the claim _does_ cover.** **A limitation that stops at what you did not do is a subtraction; one that says what the finding is therefore about has drawn a boundary, and a boundary can be relied on.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **Position before wording, and the demonstration costs four minutes.** **Write a finding on the board, then write _this opinion is subject to the limitations of a visual inspection_ two lines below it, and ask the room what the limitation applies to.** **They will say the finding.** **Then write six more findings above it and ask again.** **The answer changes, and nothing on the board has been altered** — **which is the whole mechanism and no argument is needed after it.** ⚠ **Then the quotation test, which is the cycle\'s marking instrument:** _could the other side read this aloud against me?_ **A limitation with no _therefore_ can be read twice, for you and against you. A limitation with a boundary in it can only be read for you.**'));
out.push(NOTE('**The whole-document limitation is the part that will be got wrong in the opposite direction, and it needs saying twice.** ⚠ **It exists, it is legitimate, and it goes first.** _This proposal rests on the 2019 register and therefore describes the position before the two districts were merged._ **First, the reader reads everything after it knowing what they have; last, the same sentence is a confession.** **Expect two or three students to conclude that limitations sections are forbidden** — **they are not, and the fault was never the section but the absence of a named finding.** **Where a student\'s form has a box headed _Limitations_, the instruction is to fill the box and write the real ones where they belong as well.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** _The comparison is of two dates five months apart and therefore establishes a difference and not the date on which it arose._   **2** _I have read the register in copy and not in the original; the finding is therefore about what my copy says and not about whether the register was amended._   **3** _I did not examine the welds and nothing here bears on them: the bolt findings are about diameter and a weld inspection could not change a diameter._   **4** ⚠ _This proposal rests on the 2019 register and therefore describes the position before the merger_ — **and it goes in the first paragraph.**   **5** **Open.** **The commonest answer in this class is _further work is needed_**, and the repair is to name the work, the document and the finding it would bear on.'));
