out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Zahreddine\'s last paragraph was the one quoted against him, and he had written it to be honest: this opinion is subject to the limitations of a visual inspection and to the documents made available to me, twenty-one words, and the other side read the whole of it to the tribunal twice. Mrs Tarabishi said but it is true, and every word of it is true and he would write it again — what he would not do again is put it on the last page with nothing beside it, because a limitation with no claim beside it attaches itself to everything above it, and he had seven findings above it, six of which it did not touch. Mrs Khoury said that is the whole of the cycle and it is a question of position before it is a question of wording: a limitation belongs immediately after the claim it limits, and then it is arithmetic, where on the last page it is a mood. Mrs Oueidat said the tribunal quoted it in the award. Dr Qabbani asked about the rewritten version, and seven limitations, one under each finding, each with therefore in it: the comparison is of measurements taken on two dates five months apart and therefore establishes a difference and not the date on which the difference arose, and that sentence has been quoted three times since and every time for him. Mrs Khoury said that is because therefore has to be followed by what the claim does cover — a limitation that stops at what you did not do is a subtraction, and one that says this finding is about X and not about Y has drawn a boundary, and a boundary is a thing a reader can rely on. Mr Shihabi said a desk cuts the second half, and a desk cuts the whole paragraph and should, because in copy the boundary goes inside the sentence. Mrs Ajouz said their forms have a box headed Limitations, and then fill the box and write the real ones where they belong as well, because the officer who returns your file is reading the paragraph your finding is in. Mr Tayara asked how many limitations is honest, and one for each finding, which in Mr Zahreddine\'s opinions is between four and eight, and not a list of twelve. Mrs Rizk asked about a limitation on the whole document, and then it goes first and not last, and it says what the document is therefore for. Mr Attar said that is the opposite of everything he was taught, and Mrs Tarabishi said it is the opposite of what they were all taught, and the people who mark papers, award contracts and return files all read from the top. And Mr Zahreddine said the thing he will take away is the word twice: the lawyer read it to the tribunal once to show that he was honest and once to show that nothing he had written could be relied upon, and the same twenty-one words did both jobs.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The word to keep is _twice_.** **The same twenty-one words showed that he was honest and that nothing he had written could be relied upon** — **and he had given the other side those words himself, on the last page, in good faith.**'));
