out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the most precisely shaped document in Book 1 and it should be marked against its shape before anything else.** **Numbered to the referee\'s own numbers; labelled _accepted_ or _not accepted_ in those two words; a page for every change; at least one reasoned refusal; nothing about anybody\'s tone.** **Five checks, and a letter that fails any of them fails as a document whatever its English is like.** ⚠ **The page is the one they will leave out, and the reason to insist is arithmetic rather than tidiness**: an editor with fourteen papers who cannot find the change asks the referee to find it, which is one more round for one missing number. **Mrs Tarabishi\'s first letter cost her a third round and two sentences she now has to defend in a viva.**'));
